<Layout
	title="Standard Values of Trigonometric Ratios (0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, 90°) | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Master the standard values of trigonometric ratios for 0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90° with clean value tables, memory tricks, geometric proofs, and solved examples for Class 10 Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/trigonometry" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Trigonometry</span>
			</a>

			<!-- =========================
			     LESSON HEADER
			========================= -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">04</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 04 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS</div>
					<h1>Standard <span>Values</span></h1>
					<p>
						Learn the exact values of trigonometric ratios for 0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90° with easy memory tricks, geometric proofs, and step-by-step examples.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- =========================
			     CONTENT LAYOUT
			========================= -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- =========================
					     01 · THE BASICS
					========================= -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · THE BASICS</div>
					<h2>What are Standard Values?</h2>
					<p>
						Standard values are fixed, exact numerical values of trigonometric ratios for five specific angles:
						<strong>0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90°</strong>.
					</p>
					<p>
						In Class 10 Mathematics, these five angles are fundamental because their trigonometric ratios can be derived using simple geometry without needing a calculator.
					</p>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">✓</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>Key Idea</strong>
							<p>
								Memorising standard values makes solving trigonometric expressions, heights and distances, and algebraic simplification much faster.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- =========================
					     02 · VALUE TABLE
					========================= -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · VALUE TABLE</div>
					<h2>Trigonometric Values Table</h2>
					<p>Here is the complete reference table for all 6 trigonometric ratios across the standard angles:</p>

					<div class="table-wrapper">
						<div class="value-table">
							<div class="table-row table-head">
								<div>Ratio (θ)</div>
								<div>0°</div>
								<div>30°</div>
								<div>45°</div>
								<div>60°</div>
								<div>90°</div>
							</div>

							<!-- sin -->
							<div class="table-row">
								<div class="ratio-cell"><strong>sin θ</strong></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">0</span></div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">1</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">2</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">1</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">√2</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">√3</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">2</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div><span class="value-val">1</span></div>
							</div>

							<!-- cos -->
							<div class="table-row">
								<div class="ratio-cell"><strong>cos θ</strong></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">1</span></div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">√3</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">2</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">1</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">√2</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">1</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">2</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div><span class="value-val">0</span></div>
							</div>

							<!-- tan -->
							<div class="table-row">
								<div class="ratio-cell"><strong>tan θ</strong></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">0</span></div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">1</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">√3</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div><span class="value-val">1</span></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">√3</span></div>
								<div><span class="nd-badge">Not Defined</span></div>
							</div>

							<!-- cosec -->
							<div class="table-row">
								<div class="ratio-cell"><strong>cosec θ</strong></div>
								<div><span class="nd-badge">Not Defined</span></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">2</span></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">√2</span></div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">2</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">√3</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div><span class="value-val">1</span></div>
							</div>

							<!-- sec -->
							<div class="table-row">
								<div class="ratio-cell"><strong>sec θ</strong></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">1</span></div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">2</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">√3</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div><span class="value-val">√2</span></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">2</span></div>
								<div><span class="nd-badge">Not Defined</span></div>
							</div>

							<!-- cot -->
							<div class="table-row">
								<div class="ratio-cell"><strong>cot θ</strong></div>
								<div><span class="nd-badge">Not Defined</span></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">√3</span></div>
								<div><span class="value-val">1</span></div>
								<div>
									<div class="math-fraction inline-frac">
										<span class="fraction-top">1</span>
										<span class="fraction-bottom">√3</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div><span class="value-val">0</span></div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- =========================
					     03 · MEMORY TRICK
					========================= -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · MEMORY TRICKS</div>
					<h2>How to Remember the Table Easily</h2>
					<p>You do not need to memorize all 30 values! Follow these 3 simple tricks:</p>

					<!-- Trick 1 -->
					<div class="trick-card">
						<div class="trick-badge">TRICK 1</div>
						<h3>The Square Root Pattern for Sin θ</h3>
						<p>Write numbers 0 to 4 under each angle, divide by 4, and take the square root:</p>

						<div class="pattern-grid">
							<div class="pattern-box">
								<span class="p-angle">0°</span>
								<span class="p-step">√(0 / 4)</span>
								<span class="p-result">= 0</span>
							</div>
							<div class="pattern-box">
								<span class="p-angle">30°</span>
								<span class="p-step">√(1 / 4)</span>
								<span class="p-result">= 1/2</span>
							</div>
							<div class="pattern-box">
								<span class="p-angle">45°</span>
								<span class="p-step">√(2 / 4)</span>
								<span class="p-result">= 1/√2</span>
							</div>
							<div class="pattern-box">
								<span class="p-angle">60°</span>
								<span class="p-step">√(3 / 4)</span>
								<span class="p-result">= √3/2</span>
							</div>
							<div class="pattern-box">
								<span class="p-angle">90°</span>
								<span class="p-step">√(4 / 4)</span>
								<span class="p-result">= 1</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Trick 2 & 3 Grid -->
					<div class="tricks-two-col">
						<div class="mini-trick-card">
							<div class="trick-icon">🔄</div>
							<div>
								<strong>Cos θ is Reverse of Sin θ</strong>
								<p>Just copy the <strong>sin θ</strong> values from right to left (90° down to 0°) to get all <strong>cos θ</strong> values.</p>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="mini-trick-card">
							<div class="trick-icon">➗</div>
							<div>
								<strong>Tan θ = Sin θ ÷ Cos θ</strong>
								<p>Divide the top number of sin θ by the top number of cos θ to get <strong>tan θ</strong> instantly!</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- =========================
					     04 · GEOMETRIC PROOFS
					========================= -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">04 · GEOMETRIC PROOFS</div>
					<h2>Where do these values come from?</h2>
					<p>Let's derive the values for 45°, 30°, and 60° using simple right triangles:</p>

					<!-- Proof 45° -->
					<div class="proof-card">
						<div class="proof-header">
							<span class="proof-tag">PROOF 1</span>
							<h3>Trigonometric Ratios of 45°</h3>
						</div>

						<div class="proof-body">
							<div class="proof-diagram">
								<svg viewBox="0 0 320 240" class="triangle-svg">
									<polygon points="40,200 40,40 200,200" fill="#eef4ff" stroke="#14213d" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
									<polyline points="40,175 65,175 65,200" fill="none" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="4"/>
									<!-- Angle 45 at (200,200) -->
									<path d="M 160 200 A 40 40 0 0 1 172 172" fill="none" stroke="#f4c430" stroke-width="4"/>
									<text x="145" y="185" class="svg-text">45°</text>
									<text x="25" y="125" class="svg-text">a</text>
									<text x="120" y="222" class="svg-text">a</text>
									<text x="130" y="110" class="svg-text">a√2</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<div class="proof-text">
								<p>Consider an isosceles right-angled triangle with two equal sides of length <strong>a</strong>:</p>
								<ul>
									<li>Perpendicular = <strong>a</strong></li>
									<li>Base = <strong>a</strong></li>
									<li>By Pythagoras theorem: Hypotenuse = √(a² + a²) = <strong>a√2</strong></li>
								</ul>
								<div class="proof-formula-box">
									<p><strong>sin 45°</strong> = Perpendicular / Hypotenuse = a / (a√2) = <strong>1/√2</strong></p>
									<p><strong>cos 45°</strong> = Base / Hypotenuse = a / (a√2) = <strong>1/√2</strong></p>
									<p><strong>tan 45°</strong> = Perpendicular / Base = a / a = <strong>1</strong></p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Proof 30° & 60° -->
					<div class="proof-card">
						<div class="proof-header">
							<span class="proof-tag">PROOF 2</span>
							<h3>Trigonometric Ratios of 30° and 60°</h3>
						</div>

						<div class="proof-body">
							<div class="proof-diagram">
								<svg viewBox="0 0 320 240" class="triangle-svg">
									<polygon points="60,200 60,40 220,200" fill="#eef4ff" stroke="#14213d" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
									<polyline points="60,175 85,175 85,200" fill="none" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="4"/>
									<!-- Angle 60 at bottom right -->
									<path d="M 175 200 A 45 45 0 0 1 185 167" fill="none" stroke="#f4c430" stroke-width="4"/>
									<text x="160" y="185" class="svg-text">60°</text>
									<!-- Angle 30 at top -->
									<path d="M 60 80 A 40 40 0 0 0 80 92" fill="none" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="4"/>
									<text x="75" y="115" class="svg-text">30°</text>

									<text x="40" y="125" class="svg-text">a√3</text>
									<text x="135" y="222" class="svg-text">a</text>
									<text x="150" y="110" class="svg-text">2a</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<div class="proof-text">
								<p>Consider an equilateral triangle of side <strong>2a</strong> split by an altitude:</p>
								<ul>
									<li>Base = <strong>a</strong></li>
									<li>Hypotenuse = <strong>2a</strong></li>
									<li>By Pythagoras theorem: Altitude = √((2a)² - a²) = <strong>a√3</strong></li>
								</ul>
								<div class="proof-formula-box">
									<p><strong>sin 30°</strong> = Base / Hypotenuse = a / 2a = <strong>1/2</strong></p>
									<p><strong>sin 60°</strong> = Altitude / Hypotenuse = (a√3) / 2a = <strong>√3/2</strong></p>
									<p><strong>tan 60°</strong> = Altitude / Base = (a√3) / a = <strong>√3</strong></p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- =========================
					     05 · SOLVED EXAMPLES
					========================= -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">05 · SOLVED EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Practice Problems</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Evaluate: sin 60° cos 30° + sin 30° cos 60°</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
							<p>Substitute the standard values from the table:</p>
							<ul>
								<li>sin 60° = √3/2</li>
								<li>cos 30° = √3/2</li>
								<li>sin 30° = 1/2</li>
								<li>cos 60° = 1/2</li>
							</ul>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Expression = (√3/2 × √3/2) + (1/2 × 1/2)<br/>
								= (3/4) + (1/4)<br/>
								= 4/4 = <strong>1</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2</span>
							<h3>Evaluate: 2 tan² 45° + cos² 30° - sin² 60°</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
							<ul>
								<li>tan 45° = 1 → tan² 45° = 1² = 1</li>
								<li>cos 30° = √3/2 → cos² 30° = 3/4</li>
								<li>sin 60° = √3/2 → sin² 60° = 3/4</li>
							</ul>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Expression = 2(1) + (3/4) - (3/4)<br/>
								= 2 + 0 = <strong>2</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- =========================
					     06 · SUMMARY
					========================= -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">06 · SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Quick Revision</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Standard values apply to <strong>0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90°</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Use the pattern <strong>√(n)/2</strong> for <em>n = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4</em> to get sin values.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p><strong>cos θ</strong> values are simply the reverse order of <strong>sin θ</strong> values.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>04</span>
							<p><strong>tan 90°</strong>, <strong>cosec 0°</strong>, <strong>sec 90°</strong>, and <strong>cot 0°</strong> are <em>Not Defined</em> (division by 0).</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- =========================
					     LESSON NAVIGATION
					========================= -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
